<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tirzah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tirzah was an ancient city in the northern hills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a>, usually identified with Tell el-Far'ah (North) near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nablus">Nablus</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a>. According to the Bible it served as a royal residence and the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a> from the late 10th century BCE until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omri">Omri</a> moved the seat of government to Samaria in the early 9th century BCE. Excavations show a fortified town with a long history of occupation.</p></div>
